[b]Single player only. Build 42.[/b]

Fix up a building once, then have it that way in every new game. Claim a building as your base and every tile you change is highlighted. Save the changes as a blueprint and apply it to the same building in a new game, at the start or whenever you like.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
[list]
[*]Right-click inside a building and choose Base Blueprints > Claim this building as your base, or the option that adds 6 tiles of yard.
[*]Move furniture, lay floors, paint, build or knock down walls. With Show changes on, changed tiles are gold and the claim's edge is faint blue.
[*]Open Base Blueprints... from the same menu, type a name and press Save. Only changed tiles are saved, unless you tick Save every tile.
[*]Tick Apply in new games on a blueprint, or select it and press Apply to this world. Tiles far from you are applied when you get close.
[/list]

Applying only changes what differs. Furniture that already matches stays, loot and all, and everything else on a saved tile is replaced. Container contents stay behind unless you save them with Include container contents and turn on Restore saved contents.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Blueprints are plain text files in Zomboid/Lua, so they carry over between saves.
[*]Single player only. The mod does nothing in multiplayer.
[/list]

[h2]Known issues[/h2]
[list]
[*]Not carried: trees and plants, loose items on the floor, bodies, barricades and generators.
[*]Close windows and curtains before saving. One saved open or smashed may come back that way.
[*]A door or window a zombie breaks inside the claim counts as a change, so saving removes it in the new world.
[*]Player-built doors come back without their padlock and key.
[/list]

Source and bug reports: [url=https://github.com/maxcwolf/pz-mods/tree/main/base-blueprints]GitHub[/url]
